1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,565
A planet just
rose out

2
00:00:01,565 --> 00:00:02,765
of the sea.

3
00:00:02,765 --> 00:00:04,495
Your harbor
is draining.

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,740
It's a starless
rogue,

5
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:07,880
heavy as
Jupiter,

6
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:09,810
cutting between
Earth and Mars.

7
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,380
It'll miss us.

8
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:12,880
Its gravity
won't:

9
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,300
it tugs our
oceans thirty

10
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,290
times harder
than the Moon.

11
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:18,440
Four hours
later,

12
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:19,870
the sea
comes back.

13
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,340
Then it
pulls the

14
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:23,840
Moon away
from Earth,

15
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,310
for good.

16
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:26,520
Night by
night,

17
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:27,800
the Moon
shrinks,

18
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,270
until it's just
a bright star.

19
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,230
Earth gets
dragged too.

20
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,740
Your winters
now last

21
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:35,780
five weeks
longer,

22
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:37,530
with a quarter
less sun.

23
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:39,340
It stretched
our

24
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,060
orbit into
an oval,

25
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:42,410
just like
Mars.

26
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:46,950
It never
touched us.

27
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,380
It took
our Moon,

28
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,590
and moved
our planet.
